ner":"saransh2405","html_url":"https://github.com/saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"halfak/python-para","owner":"halfak","html_url":"https://github.com/halfak/python-para","stars":1,"forks":1,"issues":1,"language":"Python","description":"a set utilities that ake advantage of python's `multiprocessing` module to distribute CPU-intensive tasks","topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"cidrblock/pyonig","owner":"cidrblock","html_url":"https://github.com/cidrblock/pyonig","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"swordofzeus/sip-of-entropy","owner":"swordofzeus","html_url":"https://github.com/swordofzeus/sip-of-entropy","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"A sip of entropy","topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"shotah/aws_fastapi_template","owner":"shotah","html_url":"https://github.com/shotah/aws_fastapi_template","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Sam CLI fastapi template","topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"glamb/sapconcur_progchal","owner":"glamb","html_url":"https://github.com/glamb/sapconcur_progchal","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":2,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"opossalite/snowflake-gen","owner":"oposs